1
00:01:42,439 --> 00:01:44,640
Wu Jinhe went to Guangzhou and isn't back yet.

2
00:01:45,719 --> 00:01:47,120
Mayor Xie went on an inspection tour to Shenzhen,

3
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:48,200
and he went along.

4
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:49,120
He won't be back until the day after tomorrow.

5
00:01:51,079 --> 00:01:52,079
Boss, to be honest...

6
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:53,959
You're the one paying my salary.

7
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:55,280
You're paying for me,

8
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:56,599
yet you have to take a cab every day.

9
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,280
Sometimes you can't even hail one,

10
00:01:58,280 --> 00:01:59,760
working day and night like this.

11
00:01:59,959 --> 00:02:01,640
The Investment Promotion Bureau has its own cars.

12
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:02,799
They don't need ours.

13
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:04,480
Isn't it exhausting working for them?

14
00:02:04,719 --> 00:02:05,840
Not like working for me,

15
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:07,079
where you can even take a nap at noon.

16
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:08,199
Not really.

17
00:02:08,599 --> 00:02:09,960
I genuinely feel for you.

18
00:02:10,199 --> 00:02:11,560
I just drive every day and sit there.

19
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:12,479
It's not like I'm pushing the car.

20
00:02:12,599 --> 00:02:14,039
I was just worried it'd be inconvenient for you.

21
00:02:17,159 --> 00:02:19,199
Isn't government work a huge hassle?

22
00:02:20,199 --> 00:02:21,280
What I mean is,

23
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,039
do you often have to deliver documents or something?

24
00:02:25,599 --> 00:02:27,159
I just drive Director Wu around every day.

25
00:02:27,159 --> 00:02:28,479
Others handle his official business.

26
00:02:28,479 --> 00:02:29,719
I mostly run personal errands.

27
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:33,439
Aren't Communist cadres dedicated to their posts day and night?

28
00:02:33,560 --> 00:02:34,759
Can public and private really be separated?

29
00:02:35,159 --> 00:02:36,719
He must work overtime every day,

30
00:02:36,719 --> 00:02:37,800
rarely going home.

31
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:39,319
Well, he keeps his belongings in the car,

32
00:02:39,319 --> 00:02:40,759
so I don't have to constantly run back to fetch them.

33
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:42,599
In this car?

34
00:02:43,439 --> 00:02:44,280
What kind of stuff?

35
00:02:45,439 --> 00:02:46,759
He took everything with him on the trip.

36
00:02:46,919 --> 00:02:48,800
Some clothes, shoes, that sort of thing.

37
00:02:48,919 --> 00:02:50,319
And he took some documents with him too.

38
00:02:51,759 --> 00:02:52,639
What documents?

39
00:02:52,919 --> 00:02:53,719
I don't know.

40
00:02:54,039 --> 00:02:55,919
Probably just some government files.

41
00:03:01,199 --> 00:03:02,360
You've been to Antique Street, right?

42
00:03:02,719 --> 00:03:03,719
I have a friend

43
00:03:03,719 --> 00:03:05,439
who opened a shop like that in Taiwan, China.

44
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:08,439
He specializes in collecting old newspapers,

45
00:03:08,439 --> 00:03:09,680
magazines, and the like.

46
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:11,560
These classified red-header files from the mainland

47
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:13,159
are rare collector's items over there too.

48
00:03:13,639 --> 00:03:15,080
It's pretty much like collecting stamps,

49
00:03:15,319 --> 00:03:16,520
but it brings in real money.

50
00:03:17,599 --> 00:03:18,599
Do you know what I mean?

51
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:35,639
Xiao Liu.

52
00:03:41,159 --> 00:03:41,719
Brother Qi.

53
00:03:41,719 --> 00:03:42,360
Thanks.

54
00:03:45,639 --> 00:03:47,199
Initial interrogation is the foundation,

55
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:48,879
surprise interrogation is the key,

56
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:50,439
and pre-trial interrogation is the safeguard.

57
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:52,639
Each step builds with clear intent.

58
00:03:54,879 --> 00:03:55,919
Different objectives,

59
00:03:55,919 --> 00:03:56,919
different timing,

60
00:03:56,919 --> 00:03:58,319
and varying levels of strategy.

61
00:04:02,479 --> 00:04:03,120
Brother Qi,

62
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:04,240
you're all right now?

63
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:06,439
Won't kill me.

64
00:04:07,439 --> 00:04:08,240
What are you writing?

65
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:17,519
Toss it out already.

66
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:20,560
I... won't mine work?

67
00:04:22,439 --> 00:04:23,920
If you want theory, stay in the research room.

68
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:24,800
Don't come to the front lines.

69
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:26,399
If book learning were all it took,

70
00:04:26,399 --> 00:04:27,480
why would we need field experience?

71
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:29,639
Every method serves the result.

72
00:04:29,639 --> 00:04:31,519
If kneeling down could get a confession,

73
00:04:31,519 --> 00:04:33,319
I'd get on my knees for Cao Liaoping right now.

74
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:34,480
I'd even kowtow to him.

75
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:36,639
What about torture then?

76
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,079
According to you,

77
00:04:38,079 --> 00:04:39,319
as long as you get results,

78
00:04:39,319 --> 00:04:40,519
anything goes?

79
00:04:40,639 --> 00:04:41,839
What is the biggest difference

80
00:04:41,839 --> 00:04:43,000
between people, essentially?

81
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:44,480
It's not about bickering.

82
00:04:44,839 --> 00:04:45,759
It's perspective.

83
00:04:46,079 --> 00:04:47,079
From a legal standpoint,

84
00:04:47,079 --> 00:04:49,560
banning torture prevents wrongful convictions.

85
00:04:49,639 --> 00:04:50,720
But during the War of Resistance?

86
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:51,720
Facing a Japanese spy who could

87
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:53,439
get your comrades killed at any second,

88
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:54,600
with lives at stake,

89
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:56,759
when so many heads hang by a thread,

90
00:04:56,759 --> 00:04:59,120
you have to target their weakest human traits.

91
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:02,600
Aren't you just twisting the argument?

92
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:04,480
That's how the adult world works.

93
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:05,639
There are many things in this world

94
00:05:05,639 --> 00:05:06,519
that aren't about right or wrong.

95
00:05:06,639 --> 00:05:08,319
What matters is which side you're on,

96
00:05:08,319 --> 00:05:09,360
and who you speak for.

97
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:10,959
Your stance comes above all.

98
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:14,680
Kid, are you working in national security,

99
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:16,879
or are you a preschool teacher grading right and wrong?

100
00:05:17,240 --> 00:05:18,439
You only brought an exercise book.

101
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:19,879
Did you bring a pencil and an eraser,

102
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:23,720
Xiao Liu?

103
00:05:30,319 --> 00:05:30,959
Come in.

104
00:05:36,839 --> 00:05:37,399
Brother Qi.

105
00:05:37,399 --> 00:05:38,319
Cao Xiao'ou is here.

106
00:05:40,439 --> 00:05:41,399
What are you doing?

107
00:05:41,399 --> 00:05:42,160
Interrogating him.

108
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:43,079
Sit down.

109
00:05:44,160 --> 00:05:44,839
What's the rush?

110
00:05:45,319 --> 00:05:46,319
It's not like he's questioning you.

111
00:05:49,759 --> 00:05:50,560
Let him stew for a bit.

112
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:55,680
If you can't sit still,

113
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:57,040
try out those theories of yours.

114
00:05:57,319 --> 00:05:59,120
Treat me as Cao Xiao'ou and give it a shot.

115
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:02,199
Today,

116
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:04,639
we are questioning you in accordance with the law.

117
00:06:04,879 --> 00:06:07,000
Our purpose is to establish the facts.

118
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,160
We expect you to state the truth.

119
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:08,959
All right, that's enough.

120
00:06:09,720 --> 00:06:10,639
I get the gist.

121
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:12,000
Save your energy.

122
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:13,319
I practiced this over and over at home.

123
00:06:13,319 --> 00:06:14,240
At this speaking pace,

124
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:15,480
he can barely get a word in edgewise.

125
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:17,240
It'll practically leave him speechless.

126
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:18,360
And then?

127
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:20,040
Applaud for you?

128
00:06:20,839 --> 00:06:22,000
That's not questioning.

129
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,519
That's a poetry recital interrogation.

130
00:06:23,639 --> 00:06:25,240
A real interrogation isn't like that either.

131
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:27,040
You need to converse, to talk.

132
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:28,160
Talk like a normal person.

133
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:29,399
Do you get what I mean?

134
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:30,600
For example?

135
00:06:32,279 --> 00:06:34,240
For instance, you must know what to say,

136
00:06:34,399 --> 00:06:35,000
what to say less of,

137
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:35,759
and what not to mention at all.

138
00:06:35,839 --> 00:06:37,480
Stick to topics within your control,

139
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:38,839
and find common ground.

140
00:06:39,759 --> 00:06:42,079
Think about what to talk about with him.

141
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:43,639
The Spring Festival Gala?

142
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:45,920
Or maybe soccer?

143
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:48,000
Then again, if we talk soccer,

144
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:49,600
can we out-talk an official from the Sports Bureau?

145
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:51,000
Any topic will do,

146
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:52,600
as long as it keeps the conversation going.

147
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:53,319
Don't let the room go cold.

148
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:54,639
The core of dialogue

149
00:06:54,639 --> 00:06:56,759
is to establish dominance in the room.

150
00:06:56,759 --> 00:06:57,600
In short:

151
00:06:58,360 --> 00:06:59,439
Whatever I want to talk about,

152
00:06:59,439 --> 00:07:00,839
you have to follow along.

153
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:01,800
Brother Qi,

154
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:05,319
could you take the lead first so I can watch?

155
00:07:06,399 --> 00:07:06,920
You question him first.

156
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:10,920
Brother Qi, my approach might not work, right?

157
00:07:12,120 --> 00:07:12,600
By the way,

158
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:14,680
72 hours is a critical threshold.

159
00:07:14,879 --> 00:07:15,800
If we go past that threshold

160
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:16,879
without a breakthrough,

161
00:07:16,879 --> 00:07:17,920
it'll only get harder and harder.

162
00:07:18,439 --> 00:07:19,800
The principle of questioning is:

163
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:22,000
they must follow your rhythm.

164
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:23,279
You have to question everything.

165
00:07:23,279 --> 00:07:25,279
Assume every single word they say is a lie.

166
00:07:25,480 --> 00:07:26,439
Understood?

167
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:50,639
What does this phrase mean?

168
00:07:51,519 --> 00:07:52,199
"When actions fail,

169
00:07:52,199 --> 00:07:53,240
look within yourself."

170
00:07:53,879 --> 00:07:55,879
It comes from Mencius's "Li Lou I."

171
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:57,800
It means that

172
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:59,879
when things don't turn out as expected,

173
00:08:00,079 --> 00:08:02,000
or when we hit setbacks and obstacles,

174
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,800
we must first reflect on ourselves

175
00:08:03,879 --> 00:08:05,560
and look for the cause within,

176
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:08,079
instead of blaming outside factors or others.

177
00:08:10,639 --> 00:08:11,639
Is there a problem with that?

178
00:08:11,879 --> 00:08:12,920
Being pedantic.

179
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:14,319
Even I can't understand it.

180
00:08:14,319 --> 00:08:15,680
Will the higher-ups be able to?

181
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:17,720
I can revise it again.

182
00:08:18,839 --> 00:08:21,360
Cao Liaoping's escape was the outcome.

183
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:24,600
The focus shouldn't be on our mistakes,

184
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:26,600
but on the complex, severe,

185
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:27,839
and volatile situation,

186
00:08:27,839 --> 00:08:29,480
and how we handled it.

187
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:31,480
If you hadn't adapted on the fly,

188
00:08:31,839 --> 00:08:33,559
it would've been much worse.

189
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:36,240
Understood.

190
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:39,039
Change "a rare misstep" to "turning the tide."

191
00:08:39,559 --> 00:08:41,320
Nitpicking words isn't the problem.

192
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,519
The problem is picking the wrong ones.

193
00:08:44,039 --> 00:08:44,600
Understood.

194
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:46,039
Make sure it's on my desk before you leave.

195
00:08:46,279 --> 00:08:46,840
Will do.

196
00:08:47,320 --> 00:08:49,200
Back when we first started training,

197
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:51,159
Deputy Chief Ding from Division Four gave us a lecture.

198
00:08:51,159 --> 00:08:53,159
He said the core of interrogation comes down to three words:

199
00:08:53,159 --> 00:08:53,799
exploit their weakness.

200
00:08:53,799 --> 00:08:55,080
Target the opponent's weakness.

201
00:08:55,360 --> 00:08:56,200
Every single question

202
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:58,000
must be framed around that idea.

203
00:08:58,440 --> 00:08:59,840
That's the true essence of interrogation.

204
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:01,120
It depends on who's interrogating,

205
00:09:01,200 --> 00:09:02,600
and who's being interrogated.

206
00:09:03,720 --> 00:09:04,759
How you ask doesn't matter.

207
00:09:04,759 --> 00:09:06,039
What matters is who's asking.

208
00:09:06,559 --> 00:09:07,360
The way I see it,

209
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:09,679
only those with real case experience,

210
00:09:10,039 --> 00:09:12,240
at least Section Chiefs or Deputy Division Chiefs,

211
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:13,799
get any real value out of training.

212
00:09:14,360 --> 00:09:16,440
For blank slates like you, it's completely pointless.

213
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:17,720
If someone tells you to exploit weaknesses,

214
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:18,679
where would you even begin?

215
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:21,759
Even the darkest paper started out blank.

216
00:09:21,759 --> 00:09:23,000
You're always looking down on rookies.

217
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,000
How else do you gain experience?

218
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:25,720
Isn't it built case by case?

219
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:26,440
Wrong.

220
00:09:27,120 --> 00:09:29,360
Go look at the neurosurgery wing at the Provincial Hospital.

221
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:31,120
Why are specialists regarded as experts?

222
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:33,120
They're naturally sharp and deft.

223
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:35,840
People who constantly scrape their cars won't cut it.

224
00:09:36,519 --> 00:09:37,879
Renowned doctors rely on talent.

225
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:39,200
Hard work is negligible.

226
00:09:39,720 --> 00:09:40,480
Do you get what I mean?

227
00:09:41,200 --> 00:09:41,879
Not really.

228
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:44,759
There are three kinds of people who run interrogations.

229
00:09:44,759 --> 00:09:45,879
First, it comes down to talent.

230
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:47,600
Some people are just naturals.

231
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:48,799
One in ten.

232
00:09:48,799 --> 00:09:49,559
Turning double agents, surprise grillings—

233
00:09:49,559 --> 00:09:51,120
they can crack major, critical cases.

234
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:52,600
When it goes smoothly, it takes less than three days.

235
00:09:52,759 --> 00:09:53,480
That's a genius.

236
00:09:53,919 --> 00:09:55,399
The second kind is capable talent.

237
00:09:55,399 --> 00:09:56,519
Sharp and quick-witted.

238
00:09:56,519 --> 00:09:58,000
They work their way up from minor cases.

239
00:09:58,080 --> 00:09:59,480
With proper training, they'll become top notch.

240
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:00,879
The third kind is just hopeless.

241
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:02,039
Simply mediocre.

242
00:10:02,039 --> 00:10:03,559
They're just not cut out for interrogation.

243
00:10:03,559 --> 00:10:04,399
Like you.

244
00:10:04,679 --> 00:10:06,600
Huadong barely counts as the second kind.

245
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:08,320
Jinlan is decent; she has potential.

246
00:10:08,519 --> 00:10:09,480
But she falls short of being a genius.

247
00:10:10,639 --> 00:10:11,759
What makes her better than us?

248
00:10:12,519 --> 00:10:14,080
Just look at the transcripts she takes.

249
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:15,639
She summarizes well and puts real thought into it.

250
00:10:15,639 --> 00:10:17,840
She doesn't just write down filler words and babble.

251
00:10:18,399 --> 00:10:19,480
Then who's a genius?

252
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:23,240
The ones who don't ask aimless questions.

253
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:24,720
Use your brain and think about it.

254
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:25,639
The person you're interrogating—

255
00:10:25,639 --> 00:10:27,039
why do they ask for water?

256
00:10:27,039 --> 00:10:27,840
When do they drink it?

257
00:10:27,840 --> 00:10:29,000
Do they drink quickly or slowly?

258
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:29,879
Are they actually thirsty?

259
00:10:29,879 --> 00:10:31,360
Or just looking for an excuse to catch their breath?

260
00:10:33,679 --> 00:10:35,120
Why do you always have so many questions?

261
00:10:38,879 --> 00:10:39,480
Xiao Yang.

262
00:10:39,799 --> 00:10:41,000
Check through all of these.

263
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:41,519
Right away.

264
00:10:47,639 --> 00:10:48,399
Sis Li,

265
00:10:48,399 --> 00:10:49,360
come over here.

266
00:10:50,240 --> 00:10:52,440
The cassette case the team found in Hong Kong, China...

267
00:10:53,159 --> 00:10:55,480
He likely used cassette cases to pass intelligence.

268
00:10:55,480 --> 00:10:56,120
Look.

269
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:05,480
Take them all back for screening.

270
00:11:09,720 --> 00:11:10,440
Here's what you do.

271
00:11:13,720 --> 00:11:14,679
Once you go inside later,

272
00:11:14,919 --> 00:11:16,919
if things aren't going smoothly,

273
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:18,240
before midnight,

274
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:19,679
take him to bed as usual.

275
00:11:19,679 --> 00:11:21,639
Then move the wall clock four hours ahead.

276
00:11:21,639 --> 00:11:23,279
Wake him back up at three a.m.

277
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:24,559
What time would that be?

278
00:11:25,519 --> 00:11:26,440
Seven in the morning.

279
00:11:27,200 --> 00:11:28,759
Bring him back and question him again.

280
00:11:28,759 --> 00:11:30,039
By seven in the evening,

281
00:11:30,039 --> 00:11:31,639
the clock will read eleven at night.

282
00:11:31,639 --> 00:11:32,720
Send him to bed again.

283
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:34,120
Let him sleep a bit, then wake him up.

284
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:35,080
Throw off his rhythm.

285
00:11:35,480 --> 00:11:36,480
Get what I mean?

286
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:39,039
Brother Qi, if we do this,

287
00:11:39,039 --> 00:11:40,320
what if Old Wei finds out?

288
00:11:41,519 --> 00:11:42,799
Why don't you go check with him?

289
00:11:46,039 --> 00:11:47,279
Get some rest. We'll take over.

290
00:11:47,279 --> 00:11:48,320
Alright, I'll leave it to you.

291
00:12:06,279 --> 00:12:07,919
Besides swimming and badminton,

292
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:11,279
you've always handled the big three, right?

293
00:12:13,039 --> 00:12:15,000
I only organize matches,

294
00:12:15,519 --> 00:12:16,679
improve performance,

295
00:12:17,039 --> 00:12:18,120
and scout talent.

296
00:12:20,120 --> 00:12:21,639
Then let's start with football.

297
00:12:21,840 --> 00:12:22,960
In the Jia-A League,

298
00:12:22,960 --> 00:12:24,840
Guangdong has four teams in total.

299
00:12:25,080 --> 00:12:26,679
Why don't we have even one?

300
00:12:28,759 --> 00:12:30,559
I'm with the municipal sports bureau,

301
00:12:30,559 --> 00:12:31,840
not the provincial one.

302
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:34,720
Besides, I'm just a minor division chief.

303
00:12:35,039 --> 00:12:36,919
A lot of things are out of my hands.

304
00:12:37,240 --> 00:12:38,600
But to the national team's coaching staff,

305
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:40,080
I did write a letter.

306
00:12:40,080 --> 00:12:41,679
It was about fitness training.

307
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:43,879
What's wrong with their fitness?

308
00:12:44,240 --> 00:12:45,679
I heard they wanted to learn from

309
00:12:45,679 --> 00:12:48,159
a certain country's training in the Euros:

310
00:12:48,720 --> 00:12:50,200
a 10,000-meter run every day.

311
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:51,679
My background is in fitness testing.

312
00:12:51,679 --> 00:12:53,360
I don't think that's scientific.

313
00:12:53,879 --> 00:12:56,279
For instance, know what you can say,

314
00:12:56,279 --> 00:12:57,639
what to say less of, and what not to say.

315
00:12:57,639 --> 00:12:59,480
Stick to topics within your control.

316
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:00,519
The core of any dialogue

317
00:13:00,519 --> 00:13:02,720
is to establish dominance in the room.

318
00:13:02,799 --> 00:13:03,919
Whatever I want to discuss,

319
00:13:03,919 --> 00:13:05,399
you must follow my lead.

320
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:08,440
Well, since you're such an expert,

321
00:13:08,799 --> 00:13:09,919
give us a prediction.

322
00:13:09,919 --> 00:13:11,840
How will the national team do in the Asian Cup?

323
00:13:12,039 --> 00:13:13,000
I can't predict that.

324
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:15,399
I can only hypothesize.

325
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,320
If I were coaching them,

326
00:13:17,600 --> 00:13:19,799
I'd have the men train with the women.

327
00:13:20,039 --> 00:13:21,080
Just think about it.

328
00:13:22,480 --> 00:13:24,720
Are the women's match tactics

329
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:26,200
ever unreasonable?

330
00:13:28,559 --> 00:13:29,240
Right.

331
00:13:30,399 --> 00:13:32,120
The women's team plays well, don't they?

332
00:13:32,879 --> 00:13:34,720
Almost beat the US team, right?

333
00:13:35,759 --> 00:13:36,399
Right.

334
00:13:36,799 --> 00:13:38,039
Have you been to the US?

335
00:13:41,120 --> 00:13:41,919
No, never.

336
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:44,080
You organized an overseas tour in March.

337
00:13:44,080 --> 00:13:45,120
Where did you go?

338
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:45,799
Japan.

339
00:13:46,399 --> 00:13:47,879
Germany and Spain.

340
00:13:48,399 --> 00:13:49,440
You've already been there.

341
00:13:49,440 --> 00:13:51,600
Why apply to visit Japan again a few days ago?

342
00:13:52,399 --> 00:13:54,240
Because they have a youth development plan,

343
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:56,399
and we can see the changes over these six months.

344
00:13:56,960 --> 00:13:59,080
What were you doing the day before applying?

345
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:01,679
Having a meeting with colleagues from work.

346
00:14:01,679 --> 00:14:02,440
Which colleagues?

347
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:03,679
What time? Where?

348
00:14:03,799 --> 00:14:04,600
It was a morning meeting.

349
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:05,720
What time, exactly?

350
00:14:08,919 --> 00:14:10,519
9:15.

351
00:14:11,799 --> 00:14:13,120
Is it like that for every meeting?

352
00:14:13,399 --> 00:14:14,480
Why wasn't it at nine?

353
00:14:14,480 --> 00:14:15,639
Was someone late,

354
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:17,480
or was it scheduled for that time?

355
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:20,679
Wait, is there a problem with that?

356
00:14:27,919 --> 00:14:30,279
If we didn't have enough evidence,

357
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:31,799
we wouldn't have gone with you to Hong Kong, China.

358
00:14:32,120 --> 00:14:34,000
You wouldn't be sitting here today,

359
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:36,600
and you wouldn't be in handcuffs.

360
00:14:38,200 --> 00:14:40,200
Still keeping your mouth shut, huh?

361
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:41,639
Not even drinking water.

362
00:14:42,039 --> 00:14:43,080
Professor Cao,

363
00:14:43,720 --> 00:14:44,960
you'll only make yourself sick.

364
00:14:51,879 --> 00:14:53,399
These minor ailments...

365
00:14:53,879 --> 00:14:55,039
can be very stubborn.

366
00:14:55,639 --> 00:14:56,840
Sometimes,

367
00:14:57,360 --> 00:14:59,879
NTU Hospital can't beat home remedies.

368
00:15:03,919 --> 00:15:07,039
Rumor has it the top brass was cured this way.

369
00:15:07,039 --> 00:15:08,480
Besides, there are no side effects.

370
00:15:08,480 --> 00:15:09,399
Why not give it a shot?

371
00:15:10,120 --> 00:15:11,120
Go ahead and sit.

372
00:15:11,879 --> 00:15:13,960
Did your hemorrhoids flare up too?

373
00:15:15,320 --> 00:15:16,480
At worst, if it doesn't work,

374
00:15:16,480 --> 00:15:18,080
it's not too late for surgery.

375
00:15:19,279 --> 00:15:20,759
What I'm worried about now is,

376
00:15:20,759 --> 00:15:21,480
tomorrow,

377
00:15:22,080 --> 00:15:23,440
when I report to the superiors.

378
00:15:23,759 --> 00:15:25,600
If they ask me to sit down,

379
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:27,200
should I sit or not?

380
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:28,360
Once I sit down,

381
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:29,480
I won't be able to stand up,

382
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:31,080
and I'll get blood all over my pants.

383
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:32,080
I'm telling you,

384
00:15:32,399 --> 00:15:33,320
good grief!

385
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:35,639
Would adult diapers...

386
00:15:35,879 --> 00:15:37,039
work as a quick fix?

387
00:15:37,039 --> 00:15:37,840
Old Zhu,

388
00:15:38,399 --> 00:15:39,279
only intelligence

389
00:15:39,440 --> 00:15:40,440
can handle an emergency.

390
00:15:40,759 --> 00:15:42,080
The Taiwan Strait situation

391
00:15:42,519 --> 00:15:43,440
is changing every day.

392
00:15:51,559 --> 00:15:54,080
What do you expect me to report to the higher-ups?

393
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:56,000
So much of the intelligence is fragmented.

394
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:56,799
And what's his name...

395
00:15:56,799 --> 00:15:57,919
Cao what's-his-face?

396
00:15:57,919 --> 00:15:58,720
Cao Liaoping.

397
00:15:58,720 --> 00:15:59,840
He didn't make it back,

398
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,000
and neither did the intel.

399
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:02,080
When on earth will

400
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:03,799
your report finally be ready?

401
00:16:05,200 --> 00:16:06,639
Before work tomorrow.

402
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:09,240
The intel brief will clarify everything.

403
00:16:09,440 --> 00:16:11,879
He's not our only asset in Institute 761.

404
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:14,320
His subordinate, or what?

405
00:16:15,399 --> 00:16:16,440
Back-to-back.

406
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:18,120
Both provide intelligence,

407
00:16:18,120 --> 00:16:19,240
cross-verifying each other.

408
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:20,879
Actually...

409
00:16:21,559 --> 00:16:23,039
this isn't what worries me.

410
00:16:26,279 --> 00:16:27,799
Stop speaking in half-sentences,

411
00:16:27,799 --> 00:16:29,960
acting like you're some big shot.

412
00:16:30,360 --> 00:16:31,679
What are you worried about? Out with it.

413
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:35,799
Regarding Cao Liaoping in Hong Kong, China...

414
00:16:35,799 --> 00:16:37,120
As for the rescue plan,

415
00:16:37,120 --> 00:16:39,320
our intel suffered a serious leak.

416
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:41,320
What I mean is...

417
00:16:41,679 --> 00:16:43,919
there's a mole in this very building.

418
00:16:49,279 --> 00:16:50,360
Are you quite finished?

419
00:16:52,399 --> 00:16:55,799
Everyone at that meeting was deputy director or above.

420
00:16:55,799 --> 00:16:57,399
No more than six people, including me.

421
00:16:57,399 --> 00:16:58,759
We had barely served the dishes here,

422
00:16:58,759 --> 00:17:01,200
and the Communists in Hong Kong, China were already feasting.

423
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:06,599
Director, I need authorization for an internal probe.

424
00:17:08,880 --> 00:17:12,680
Also, that guy called Ma Qi, right?

425
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:14,599
Didn't your people meet with him?

426
00:17:16,119 --> 00:17:17,480
What was his attitude?

427
00:17:33,480 --> 00:17:35,079
Cao Xiao'ou, wake up. Wake up.

428
00:17:35,079 --> 00:17:35,720
Get up.

429
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:37,119
Do you like the breakfast here?

430
00:17:37,119 --> 00:17:38,279
Which team is your favorite?

431
00:17:38,599 --> 00:17:40,359
Which teams played in that match?

432
00:17:40,359 --> 00:17:42,079
Didn't you say earlier you met Cao Liaoping?

433
00:17:42,079 --> 00:17:44,039
Mr. Cao, you must tell everything you know,

434
00:17:44,039 --> 00:17:45,400
everything about your uncle,

435
00:17:45,400 --> 00:17:46,640
in full and clear detail.

436
00:17:47,279 --> 00:17:48,880
Only then will you get through this.

437
00:17:49,839 --> 00:17:50,720
Time and place.

438
00:17:50,720 --> 00:17:51,920
What did you just have for dinner?

439
00:17:53,920 --> 00:17:54,599
But didn't you say

440
00:17:54,599 --> 00:17:56,240
you wrote them a letter?

441
00:17:56,680 --> 00:17:58,480
You led an overseas tour this March.

442
00:17:58,480 --> 00:17:59,119
Where did you go?

443
00:17:59,119 --> 00:18:00,319
Where did you meet Cao Liaoping?

444
00:18:01,599 --> 00:18:02,279
Meet?

445
00:18:03,039 --> 00:18:03,720
Did you meet him?

446
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:05,400
Yes, you said so yourself just now.

447
00:18:05,400 --> 00:18:06,240
What time? Where?

448
00:18:06,240 --> 00:18:06,839
What did you discuss?

449
00:18:07,119 --> 00:18:08,519
Did I take my blood pressure pills?

450
00:18:09,920 --> 00:18:11,359
Cao Xiao'ou, let's go.

451
00:18:11,880 --> 00:18:12,480
Where to?

452
00:18:12,480 --> 00:18:13,519
Next door. Questioning.

453
00:18:13,680 --> 00:18:15,240
What did you do the day before applying?

454
00:18:15,240 --> 00:18:17,000
Why did he push you to go on overseas trips?

455
00:18:17,079 --> 00:18:17,920
Where did he tell you to go?

456
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:19,240
Let me sleep a little longer.

457
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:21,319
I've confessed everything I know.

458
00:18:28,599 --> 00:18:29,920
What did you just ask me?

459
00:18:30,480 --> 00:18:31,799
Did I fall asleep?

460
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:36,720
I just couldn't hold out anymore.

461
00:18:37,920 --> 00:18:39,640
Repeatedly asking someone the same questions...

462
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:40,839
What have you learned from that?

463
00:18:41,359 --> 00:18:43,599
If this person is telling the truth,

464
00:18:43,599 --> 00:18:45,440
they will rephrase their words

465
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:47,000
to recount what happened that day.

466
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,720
If this person is lying,

467
00:18:48,799 --> 00:18:50,279
they will repeat it word for word.

468
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:52,039
Because they prepared in advance.

469
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:55,799
Unless it's a rehearsed script learned by heart.

470
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:56,839
Especially when sleep-deprived,

471
00:18:56,839 --> 00:18:58,200
and their mind is confused.

472
00:18:59,279 --> 00:19:01,079
Tampering with clocks, round-the-clock shifts...

473
00:19:01,079 --> 00:19:02,720
It breaks standard investigation procedures.

474
00:19:02,720 --> 00:19:04,200
Old Wei will find out sooner or later.

475
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:09,240
That's why you separate "sooner" from "later."

476
00:19:09,599 --> 00:19:10,640
You can't let leadership make mistakes,

477
00:19:10,640 --> 00:19:11,880
nor can you let leadership take the blame.

478
00:19:12,240 --> 00:19:13,839
So when it comes to mistakes and blame,

479
00:19:13,839 --> 00:19:14,920
I take it all on myself.

480
00:19:15,440 --> 00:19:17,279
That's why on many things, you can't ask.

481
00:19:17,519 --> 00:19:18,799
You can't put leadership in a bind.

482
00:19:19,240 --> 00:19:19,880
Be sensible.

483
00:19:20,319 --> 00:19:22,200
Don't you want to get promoted?

484
00:19:22,440 --> 00:19:23,720
Playing with semantics like this...

485
00:19:23,720 --> 00:19:24,880
Won't leadership reprimand you?

486
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:25,880
Why would he reprimand me?

487
00:19:26,039 --> 00:19:27,480
Isn't a capable subordinate a good thing?

488
00:19:28,079 --> 00:19:29,200
If I had known earlier,

489
00:19:29,200 --> 00:19:30,279
I wouldn't have dared to pick you.

490
00:19:32,519 --> 00:19:33,960
Why do you think I picked you?

491
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:35,359
Because I knew long ago

492
00:19:35,359 --> 00:19:36,880
that only you share my blood type.

493
00:19:37,079 --> 00:19:38,200
If I had picked someone else,

494
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:39,640
who could give me a transfusion in Hong Kong, China?

495
00:19:43,799 --> 00:19:45,160
Tell me the truth. Are you afraid of dying?

496
00:19:47,400 --> 00:19:48,079
Of course I am.

497
00:19:48,079 --> 00:19:49,000
More than anyone.

498
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:50,000
Tell me, who isn't afraid?

499
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:50,599
You?

500
00:19:51,759 --> 00:19:53,279
In this line of work, you die on the front line.

501
00:20:15,319 --> 00:20:16,240
I have a question

502
00:20:16,839 --> 00:20:17,960
I've always wanted to ask you.

503
00:20:21,079 --> 00:20:21,880
Don't ask.

504
00:20:25,079 --> 00:20:26,640
The person you met in Hong Kong, China—

505
00:20:26,960 --> 00:20:28,119
was that your informant?

506
00:20:28,960 --> 00:20:31,000
You just need to answer yes or no.

507
00:20:37,039 --> 00:20:38,079
Everyone else suspected me.

508
00:20:38,519 --> 00:20:39,680
Only you never doubted me.

509
00:20:39,960 --> 00:20:40,839
Old Wei said

510
00:20:41,359 --> 00:20:43,240
you told him you didn't believe I was a traitor.

511
00:20:43,799 --> 00:20:45,000
And I don't believe you are, either.

512
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:58,160
Do you think informants are reliable?

513
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:00,880
If not,

514
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:02,559
why take the risk to meet him?

515
00:21:08,359 --> 00:21:09,440
The leaders always say

516
00:21:10,079 --> 00:21:12,079
informants are turned from the enemy camp,

517
00:21:12,359 --> 00:21:14,279
so stay alert and don't get emotional.

518
00:21:14,960 --> 00:21:16,759
But I never treat an informant as just an informant.

519
00:21:17,960 --> 00:21:19,599
From the day we become friends,

520
00:21:19,599 --> 00:21:21,119
I treat him like a brother.

521
00:21:21,319 --> 00:21:22,200
Even if he betrays me,

522
00:21:22,200 --> 00:21:23,279
he's still a brother.

523
00:21:23,680 --> 00:21:25,759
You have to force your mind to think that way

524
00:21:26,079 --> 00:21:27,400
to truly connect with him.

525
00:21:30,599 --> 00:21:32,319
People are the hardest thing to manage in this world.

526
00:21:32,839 --> 00:21:34,599
So you must offer your heart first.

527
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:36,759
You must treat him as a confidant,

528
00:21:37,160 --> 00:21:38,000
as a friend,

529
00:21:38,359 --> 00:21:39,480
as a life-and-death bond.

530
00:21:39,960 --> 00:21:42,759
Genuine feelings work better than live ammo.

531
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:45,640
And that's the only way.

532
00:21:48,839 --> 00:21:49,960
What about Cao Xiao'ou?

533
00:21:50,480 --> 00:21:52,160
If he wants to be your informant,

534
00:21:52,160 --> 00:21:53,200
would you share a life-and-death bond with him?

535
00:21:58,960 --> 00:22:00,000
15 minutes are up.

536
00:22:00,759 --> 00:22:02,880
Let's go wake up that "life-and-death" friend.

537
00:22:03,200 --> 00:22:04,920
He's slept long enough. Time to continue.

538
00:22:06,119 --> 00:22:07,599
Triangle cake,

539
00:22:08,839 --> 00:22:10,400
peanut soup,

540
00:22:10,400 --> 00:22:12,279
Zixi rice noodles,

541
00:22:12,519 --> 00:22:14,000
and a side dish.

542
00:22:14,240 --> 00:22:15,039
What else do you want?

543
00:22:15,039 --> 00:22:15,799
Want a marinated egg?

544
00:22:16,799 --> 00:22:17,440
Yeah.

545
00:22:17,799 --> 00:22:18,640
What about Guangbing?

546
00:22:18,799 --> 00:22:19,599
That too.

547
00:22:20,599 --> 00:22:21,640
Double-bag them, please.

548
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:22,880
Division Chief Cao likes his food hot.

549
00:22:42,680 --> 00:22:44,640
Whether we can still call you Division Chief

550
00:22:44,640 --> 00:22:46,599
depends on the outcome of this investigation.

551
00:22:47,400 --> 00:22:48,039
Think it through.

552
00:22:48,599 --> 00:22:49,839
Don't leave out a single detail.

553
00:22:50,599 --> 00:22:52,279
But with some things,

554
00:22:55,839 --> 00:22:57,880
I don't even know if they're a problem.

555
00:22:58,400 --> 00:22:58,960
Say it anyway.

556
00:22:59,519 --> 00:23:00,559
Only then will we know.

557
00:23:01,519 --> 00:23:03,880
If... If I talk,

558
00:23:05,119 --> 00:23:06,519
what can you guarantee?

559
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:10,920
Favorable treatment for your uncle,

560
00:23:11,160 --> 00:23:12,839
and at least cutting his sentence in half.

561
00:23:14,119 --> 00:23:15,160
I swear by this light.

562
00:23:24,319 --> 00:23:25,599
I want to see your supervisor.

563
00:23:25,599 --> 00:23:26,720
He's already next door,

564
00:23:27,039 --> 00:23:27,759
waiting for you

565
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:35,559
to confess.

566
00:24:03,440 --> 00:24:04,240
Brother Qi,

567
00:24:05,480 --> 00:24:07,119
we're not the court.

568
00:24:07,319 --> 00:24:09,160
How can we decide the sentence length?

569
00:24:11,480 --> 00:24:13,039
If he were as smart as you,

570
00:24:13,319 --> 00:24:14,599
he wouldn't have been conned like that.

571
00:24:14,839 --> 00:24:16,319
His uncle won't get any special treatment.

572
00:24:16,319 --> 00:24:17,759
If the damage is severe enough,

573
00:24:17,759 --> 00:24:18,920
it's at least ten years.

574
00:24:20,160 --> 00:24:21,720
Then aren't you deceiving him?

575
00:24:22,160 --> 00:24:23,880
Didn't you teach me before

576
00:24:23,880 --> 00:24:25,720
to form a life-and-death bond with informants?

577
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:28,480
Well, informants are ranked in tiers.

578
00:24:29,200 --> 00:24:30,599
When you buy fish and shrimp at the market,

579
00:24:30,599 --> 00:24:31,319
the cheap and the expensive

580
00:24:31,319 --> 00:24:32,559
aren't put side by side, right?

581
00:24:32,720 --> 00:24:34,200
Why are you willing to spend more on lobster?

582
00:24:34,599 --> 00:24:35,759
Because it tastes good, obviously.

583
00:24:36,039 --> 00:24:36,759
Isn't that right?

584
00:24:42,200 --> 00:24:42,880
I stayed up too late.

585
00:24:42,880 --> 00:24:43,960
Even if I lie down, I can't sleep.

586
00:24:44,359 --> 00:24:46,039
Let's check out the pricier one next door.

587
00:24:54,960 --> 00:24:56,079
He doesn't drink much water.

588
00:24:57,000 --> 00:24:58,920
His hands are steady when holding the cup.

589
00:24:59,279 --> 00:25:00,839
I heard he won't answer any questions.

590
00:25:01,359 --> 00:25:02,839
Apart from eating and using the restroom,

591
00:25:02,839 --> 00:25:03,920
he barely speaks.

592
00:25:04,440 --> 00:25:05,920
He doesn't make demands about his meals,

593
00:25:06,400 --> 00:25:08,640
isn't anxious, and hasn't asked for the time.

594
00:25:09,559 --> 00:25:11,559
Besides, his leather shoes are very clean.

595
00:25:11,920 --> 00:25:14,519
That means he cares about his appearance and dignity.

596
00:25:15,240 --> 00:25:16,759
Quite the theorist, aren't you?

597
00:25:18,160 --> 00:25:18,720
Brother Qi,

598
00:25:19,079 --> 00:25:21,599
I learned this during recruit training,

599
00:25:21,599 --> 00:25:23,359
but when putting it into practice,

600
00:25:23,880 --> 00:25:25,119
it doesn't seem very effective.

601
00:25:25,400 --> 00:25:27,000
Is it because I lack experience?

602
00:25:27,400 --> 00:25:29,480
Don't sell yourself short. Keep going.

603
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:30,839
Teach me something.

604
00:25:30,839 --> 00:25:32,599
How many types of suspects sit in there?

605
00:25:33,640 --> 00:25:36,359
Psychologically, they fall into five levels.

606
00:25:36,359 --> 00:25:37,599
The first group to confess

607
00:25:37,599 --> 00:25:39,039
usually can't let go of

608
00:25:39,039 --> 00:25:40,799
their status in society,

609
00:25:41,119 --> 00:25:42,400
their jobs, or identities.

610
00:25:42,519 --> 00:25:44,440
Those with weaker psychological resilience

611
00:25:44,440 --> 00:25:45,480
break down right away.

612
00:25:45,759 --> 00:25:47,599
The second type is similar to the first,

613
00:25:47,759 --> 00:25:49,160
but they care more about freedom.

614
00:25:49,359 --> 00:25:52,720
To get a lighter sentence for themselves or family,

615
00:25:53,079 --> 00:25:53,880
they can easily

616
00:25:53,880 --> 00:25:55,359
be broken down at this stage too.

617
00:25:55,559 --> 00:25:56,559
Like Cao Xiao'ou.

618
00:25:58,440 --> 00:25:59,160
Go on.

619
00:25:59,640 --> 00:26:00,920
As for the third type,

620
00:26:00,920 --> 00:26:02,119
they care more about family.

621
00:26:02,400 --> 00:26:04,000
To protect their family and children,

622
00:26:04,319 --> 00:26:06,160
they'll yield at this stage.

623
00:26:06,400 --> 00:26:07,920
The fourth type is the most common.

624
00:26:08,279 --> 00:26:09,440
Nothing matters more than their life.

625
00:26:09,599 --> 00:26:10,720
When facing life and death,

626
00:26:10,720 --> 00:26:12,440
very few can pass that test.

627
00:26:13,960 --> 00:26:14,559
Brother Qi,

628
00:26:14,880 --> 00:26:17,319
which type do you think Cao Liaoping is?

629
00:26:17,519 --> 00:26:18,240
How should we interrogate him?

630
00:26:18,799 --> 00:26:20,119
Aren't you the theorist here?

631
00:26:20,480 --> 00:26:22,039
I'm still waiting for you to teach me.

632
00:26:57,400 --> 00:26:59,240
Ballistic missile launch methods,

633
00:26:59,240 --> 00:27:00,480
based on launch platforms,

634
00:27:00,480 --> 00:27:02,759
can be divided into land-based and sea-based.

635
00:27:03,599 --> 00:27:04,960
Among them, for sea-based launches,

636
00:27:05,279 --> 00:27:06,640
all nuclear powers adopt

637
00:27:06,640 --> 00:27:09,119
submarine underwater missile launches.

638
00:27:10,119 --> 00:27:13,200
Ballistic missile nuclear submarines have high speed,

639
00:27:13,559 --> 00:27:14,359
strong endurance,

640
00:27:14,359 --> 00:27:15,319
long cruising range,

641
00:27:15,799 --> 00:27:17,240
and can stay hidden underwater for a long time.

642
00:27:18,279 --> 00:27:19,640
Refueled once with nuclear fuel,

643
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:21,720
they can operate continuously for three to seven years,

644
00:27:22,160 --> 00:27:24,160
cruising 60,000 to 300,000 nautical miles,

645
00:27:24,759 --> 00:27:26,559
with a diving depth of 300...

646
00:27:26,960 --> 00:27:28,799
We've already laid the evidence out on the table.

647
00:27:29,720 --> 00:27:31,319
We're playing with all our cards face up now.

648
00:27:31,720 --> 00:27:32,440
Talk to us.

649
00:27:36,640 --> 00:27:39,319
Colluding with foreign institutions, organizations, and individuals,

650
00:27:39,599 --> 00:27:40,960
endangering national sovereignty,

651
00:27:41,359 --> 00:27:42,839
territorial integrity, and security—

652
00:27:43,160 --> 00:27:44,000
this is a felony.

653
00:27:44,319 --> 00:27:45,240
It carries life imprisonment

654
00:27:45,240 --> 00:27:46,799
or a fixed term of over ten years.

655
00:27:47,079 --> 00:27:49,440
If the harm to the nation and the people is extreme

656
00:27:49,559 --> 00:27:50,759
and the circumstances are particularly egregious,

657
00:27:51,200 --> 00:27:52,519
it can carry the death penalty.

658
00:27:55,559 --> 00:27:56,920
Don't you have anything to say?

659
00:28:05,480 --> 00:28:07,839
Cao Xiao'ou was just like you in the beginning.

660
00:28:08,400 --> 00:28:10,359
Not unwilling to talk, but afraid to.

661
00:28:11,079 --> 00:28:13,559
Not knowing if he'd say too much or too little,

662
00:28:13,559 --> 00:28:15,839
or whether it'd help him or put him at a disadvantage.

663
00:28:16,480 --> 00:28:18,079
But once everything was laid bare,

664
00:28:18,559 --> 00:28:19,240
looking back,

665
00:28:19,240 --> 00:28:20,240
you'll realize

666
00:28:20,640 --> 00:28:22,440
it's just like looking back at what you did in elementary

667
00:28:22,440 --> 00:28:24,319
and middle school.

668
00:28:24,799 --> 00:28:26,039
Blinded in the moment,

669
00:28:26,039 --> 00:28:27,039
totally pointless.

670
00:28:27,519 --> 00:28:29,119
You'll end up talking anyway,

671
00:28:29,359 --> 00:28:30,839
so why not speak up sooner?

672
00:28:33,920 --> 00:28:35,720
Of course, that's human nature.

673
00:28:36,240 --> 00:28:37,039
If I were you,

674
00:28:37,039 --> 00:28:38,880
sitting here, my heart would be pounding too.

675
00:28:39,079 --> 00:28:42,559
Don't you think research and second-guessing are a lot alike?

676
00:28:43,400 --> 00:28:44,759
You don't know what the outcome will be,

677
00:28:45,480 --> 00:28:47,160
nor how long the process takes.

678
00:28:47,720 --> 00:28:49,319
All you can do is suffer through it.

679
00:28:49,599 --> 00:28:51,440
A researcher friend of mine once told me

680
00:28:51,440 --> 00:28:53,480
that scientific research can be tough,

681
00:28:54,000 --> 00:28:55,440
but it can also be simple.

682
00:28:55,720 --> 00:28:58,039
Sometimes, it's just a matter of piercing a thin veil.

683
00:28:58,319 --> 00:29:00,799
When I was a kid, I read a popular science book.

684
00:29:01,039 --> 00:29:01,279
In it...

685
00:29:01,279 --> 00:29:04,160
You're actually in agony right now, aren't you?

686
00:29:31,119 --> 00:29:32,720
Comrade, we're from Municipal State Security.

687
00:29:32,720 --> 00:29:34,400
We cleared it with your security office.

688
00:29:34,759 --> 00:29:35,480
We're here for an inspection.

689
00:29:37,880 --> 00:29:38,599
Please sign in.

690
00:29:38,799 --> 00:29:39,279
All right.

691
00:29:41,720 --> 00:29:43,039
Comrade, we're from Municipal State Security.

692
00:29:43,119 --> 00:29:44,720
We cleared it with your security office.

693
00:29:45,640 --> 00:29:46,440
Follow me.

694
00:29:58,400 --> 00:29:59,000
Professor Jia.

695
00:29:59,720 --> 00:30:01,039
Come in, please come in.

696
00:30:01,039 --> 00:30:02,799
Hello. State Security Bureau.

697
00:30:03,279 --> 00:30:04,759
Xiao Li already told me.

698
00:30:04,759 --> 00:30:06,200
Have a seat. No one's over there.

699
00:30:06,200 --> 00:30:06,559
All right.

700
00:30:06,559 --> 00:30:07,119
Make yourself at home.

701
00:30:08,920 --> 00:30:09,920
The reason we're here today...

702
00:30:09,920 --> 00:30:10,920
...is mainly to learn about...

703
00:30:10,920 --> 00:30:12,599
...Professor Cao Liaoping's situation.

704
00:30:12,599 --> 00:30:14,000
You were college classmates before.

705
00:30:14,160 --> 00:30:14,880
Yes, that's right.

706
00:30:14,880 --> 00:30:17,039
And you've always shared this office.

707
00:30:17,240 --> 00:30:18,559
Exactly. And he...

708
00:30:18,799 --> 00:30:19,960
...sat right where you are now.

709
00:30:20,920 --> 00:30:21,799
All right, thank you.

710
00:30:23,799 --> 00:30:24,319
Go ahead and answer it.

711
00:30:24,559 --> 00:30:25,440
We can step outside.

712
00:30:30,079 --> 00:30:30,759
It's fine.

713
00:30:32,440 --> 00:30:33,160
Please go on.

714
00:30:35,400 --> 00:30:36,720
We'd like to know about Professor Cao's...

715
00:30:36,720 --> 00:30:38,599
...recent state of work.

716
00:30:39,039 --> 00:30:41,839
Such as his relations with colleagues,

717
00:30:42,119 --> 00:30:43,400
his enthusiasm for work,

718
00:30:43,519 --> 00:30:44,480
and things in general.

719
00:30:44,480 --> 00:30:47,200
Has anything changed compared to before?

720
00:30:48,519 --> 00:30:49,039
Comrade,

721
00:30:49,880 --> 00:30:50,799
about what he did...

722
00:30:51,160 --> 00:30:52,720
did you know about it long ago,

723
00:30:52,720 --> 00:30:53,960
or did you just find out?

724
00:30:54,079 --> 00:30:54,799
What do you mean?

725
00:30:56,640 --> 00:30:58,720
Even if you hadn't come,

726
00:30:58,920 --> 00:31:00,759
I would have reported him myself.

727
00:31:01,599 --> 00:31:02,720
I can be a witness.

728
00:31:03,640 --> 00:31:04,319
If for nothing else,

729
00:31:04,720 --> 00:31:05,480
then for our institute,

730
00:31:06,119 --> 00:31:07,200
for our conglomerate,

731
00:31:07,480 --> 00:31:09,119
and for our national security.

732
00:31:24,279 --> 00:31:24,799
Eat up.

733
00:31:25,400 --> 00:31:26,160
It'll get soggy soon.

734
00:31:33,359 --> 00:31:34,160
What's on your mind?

735
00:31:37,319 --> 00:31:39,039
Can't crack a tough nut like him?

736
00:31:41,279 --> 00:31:42,079
Which type is he, really?

737
00:31:42,079 --> 00:31:42,920
Did you figure it out?

738
00:31:43,880 --> 00:31:45,559
Still refusing to confess or admit anything...

739
00:31:45,559 --> 00:31:46,759
...means he's the fifth type.

740
00:31:47,000 --> 00:31:48,319
This type is the hardest to interrogate.

741
00:31:48,519 --> 00:31:49,720
Because they're not afraid of death.

742
00:31:50,039 --> 00:31:52,319
What they care about is dignity and pride.

743
00:31:52,799 --> 00:31:55,079
When someone isn't even afraid of dying,

744
00:31:55,079 --> 00:31:56,240
how do you even interrogate them?

745
00:31:57,319 --> 00:31:58,359
Pretty sharp analysis.

746
00:31:58,519 --> 00:31:59,440
So what do you plan to do?

747
00:32:00,960 --> 00:32:01,559
Brother Qi,

748
00:32:01,920 --> 00:32:03,720
why do you always make me question him first?

749
00:32:04,240 --> 00:32:05,640
With my weak skills,

750
00:32:05,640 --> 00:32:07,000
aren't you afraid we'll lose the upper hand?

751
00:32:07,640 --> 00:32:08,519
Next week,

752
00:32:09,200 --> 00:32:10,799
the provincial department is holding a sports meet.

753
00:32:11,039 --> 00:32:11,839
Entries are mandatory.

754
00:32:12,200 --> 00:32:13,400
In the 4x200-meter relay,

755
00:32:13,759 --> 00:32:14,880
you're running the first leg.

756
00:32:14,880 --> 00:32:16,119
To test the competition.

757
00:32:16,799 --> 00:32:17,599
Interrogations work the same way.

758
00:32:17,960 --> 00:32:19,039
Then why aren't you running?

759
00:32:19,839 --> 00:32:21,720
The head coach's role is obviously far more important.

760
00:32:22,720 --> 00:32:24,480
Besides, I haven't fully recovered yet.

761
00:32:26,000 --> 00:32:27,400
Trying to kill me off and take my place?

762
00:32:35,119 --> 00:32:35,640
Brother Qi,

763
00:32:36,079 --> 00:32:37,759
why do I have two eggs?

764
00:32:37,759 --> 00:32:38,759
You're still recovering,

765
00:32:39,079 --> 00:32:39,920
so you should have the extra one.

766
00:32:40,160 --> 00:32:42,039
This is the best you get on your birthday.

767
00:32:42,279 --> 00:32:43,240
Still better than what most get.

768
00:32:43,359 --> 00:32:44,400
Just think of it as longevity noodles.

769
00:32:44,480 --> 00:32:45,319
Make do with it.

770
00:32:45,599 --> 00:32:47,720
How did you remember it's my birthday?

771
00:32:48,119 --> 00:32:49,359
You even remembered a detail like that.

772
00:32:50,319 --> 00:32:51,559
The union sent a notice.

773
00:32:52,160 --> 00:32:53,519
You're not my girlfriend,

774
00:32:53,519 --> 00:32:54,720
and you're not a suspect.

775
00:32:54,880 --> 00:32:55,960
Why would I remember that?

776
00:32:56,839 --> 00:32:57,400
Brother Qi,

777
00:32:58,079 --> 00:32:59,519
what if he never confesses?

778
00:32:59,720 --> 00:33:01,279
Do we just keep dragging this out with him?

779
00:33:02,720 --> 00:33:03,880
Eat up and go to sleep.

780
00:33:04,480 --> 00:33:05,920
Don't wake me unless the sky falls.

781
00:33:17,480 --> 00:33:18,519
Boss, take a look.

782
00:33:19,000 --> 00:33:20,599
These are apartments,

783
00:33:20,599 --> 00:33:23,000
and this one's a single-story house.

784
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:25,160
These are all new listings I found.

785
00:33:25,559 --> 00:33:29,480
And this is a newly built villa.

786
00:33:29,480 --> 00:33:33,039
The agent said it's the only one downtown.

787
00:33:33,039 --> 00:33:35,640
Boss, it's for sale only, not rent.

788
00:33:35,640 --> 00:33:37,359
I already left my number.

789
00:33:37,599 --> 00:33:38,920
If you're interested,

790
00:33:38,920 --> 00:33:40,400
I can go check it out anytime.

791
00:33:40,559 --> 00:33:41,559
After searching for so long,

792
00:33:41,559 --> 00:33:42,759
each place is worse than the last.

793
00:33:43,880 --> 00:33:45,079
Go to this address.

794
00:33:45,680 --> 00:33:47,119
I've already seen the place.

795
00:33:47,359 --> 00:33:48,920
Just go ahead and rent it.

796
00:33:49,240 --> 00:33:51,359
Boss, that place is really far.

797
00:33:51,359 --> 00:33:53,839
Think how much more you'll spend on gas each day.

798
00:33:53,839 --> 00:33:55,119
If I wanted to save money,

799
00:33:55,119 --> 00:33:57,039
I'd just sleep at the office.

800
00:33:57,599 --> 00:33:59,400
I really like this place. It's the one.

801
00:33:59,720 --> 00:34:01,119
The landlord isn't local either.

802
00:34:01,559 --> 00:34:02,480
If they ask on the phone,

803
00:34:02,480 --> 00:34:04,039
tell them you'll be living there yourself.

804
00:34:04,200 --> 00:34:06,039
Students don't need to register, and it's cheaper.

805
00:34:06,359 --> 00:34:07,559
If you're not in a hurry,

806
00:34:07,559 --> 00:34:08,840
I think we can get a better price.

807
00:34:09,159 --> 00:34:10,519
Let me go haggle with them.

808
00:34:13,119 --> 00:34:15,920
Don't cut corners where you shouldn't.

809
00:34:17,360 --> 00:34:18,960
Talk to them first—

810
00:34:19,199 --> 00:34:20,519
one month's deposit, three months' rent.

811
00:34:21,239 --> 00:34:22,039
If...

812
00:34:22,719 --> 00:34:24,880
if worse comes to worst, sign for six months.

813
00:34:24,880 --> 00:34:25,880
Six months.

814
00:34:26,719 --> 00:34:27,760
Either way, I have only one requirement:

815
00:34:27,760 --> 00:34:28,679
you must close the deal,

816
00:34:28,679 --> 00:34:29,719
and don't blow it.

817
00:34:29,719 --> 00:34:30,519
Got it.

818
00:34:31,280 --> 00:34:31,920
Boss,

819
00:34:32,159 --> 00:34:34,360
what about your old place?

820
00:34:34,360 --> 00:34:36,079
How about I find someone to sublet it?

821
00:34:36,360 --> 00:34:38,360
That way it'll be a seamless transition,

822
00:34:38,599 --> 00:34:40,519
and we can save every penny we can.

823
00:34:41,920 --> 00:34:44,039
Have you drawn up the Dingxiang Hospital contract?

824
00:34:44,360 --> 00:34:45,159
It's ready.

825
00:34:55,760 --> 00:34:57,199
Don't give up the old place.

826
00:34:57,480 --> 00:34:58,360
Leave it for now.

827
00:34:59,159 --> 00:35:00,760
Just rent the new one first.

828
00:35:06,679 --> 00:35:09,280
Brother Qi, it's been checked three times.

829
00:35:09,760 --> 00:35:12,800
They even brought in the sleeper Queen Ant.

830
00:35:13,440 --> 00:35:15,360
And Old Wei led the team himself.

831
00:35:15,360 --> 00:35:16,760
They couldn't have missed anything.

832
00:35:17,840 --> 00:35:18,679
We have to check.

833
00:35:57,440 --> 00:35:59,360
Why did he collect so much of this stuff?

834
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:01,039
What's all this for?

835
00:36:22,800 --> 00:36:23,639
What medicine is this?

836
00:36:45,199 --> 00:36:46,480
Brother Qi, where have you been?

837
00:36:46,880 --> 00:36:47,880
Why is there liquor too?

838
00:36:48,280 --> 00:36:48,840
Sorry about that.

839
00:36:48,840 --> 00:36:49,679
Forgot to ask for permission.

840
00:36:49,920 --> 00:36:51,280
I'll give you a full report later.

841
00:36:52,800 --> 00:36:53,519
Help me open this.

842
00:37:10,239 --> 00:37:11,599
I don't usually drink red wine,

843
00:37:11,599 --> 00:37:12,159
so I don't know much about it.

844
00:37:12,440 --> 00:37:13,239
Anyway,

845
00:37:13,360 --> 00:37:15,280
I got it from the shop you always go to.

846
00:37:15,679 --> 00:37:16,440
What's going on?

847
00:37:16,880 --> 00:37:18,039
Changing up the tactics.

848
00:37:18,559 --> 00:37:19,920
It's the priciest one from Germany.

849
00:37:20,320 --> 00:37:22,159
Glasses and cutlery aren't allowed in,

850
00:37:22,320 --> 00:37:23,679
and the white towel tucked around your neck—

851
00:37:23,679 --> 00:37:24,559
that would've been allowed,

852
00:37:25,079 --> 00:37:25,480
but I forgot it.

853
00:37:26,039 --> 00:37:26,599
You'll have to make do.

854
00:37:30,280 --> 00:37:31,360
Your wife just fell asleep.

855
00:37:31,760 --> 00:37:32,960
She's been a bit worn out lately,

856
00:37:33,119 --> 00:37:34,159
but she's holding up fine.

857
00:37:34,400 --> 00:37:34,960
Hasn't broken down.

858
00:37:35,400 --> 00:37:36,599
After all, she knows nothing.

859
00:37:36,880 --> 00:37:37,599
She's an outsider, of course.

860
00:37:37,880 --> 00:37:39,679
Doesn't need to overthink anything.

861
00:37:39,920 --> 00:37:41,480
Your nephew isn't handling it quite as well.

862
00:37:41,920 --> 00:37:42,920
His blood pressure is a bit high.

863
00:37:43,480 --> 00:37:44,039
Heart palpitations.

864
00:37:44,840 --> 00:37:45,599
The doctor checked him out.

865
00:37:45,800 --> 00:37:47,079
Said it's anxiety.

866
00:37:47,480 --> 00:37:48,320
Just temporary.

867
00:37:50,679 --> 00:37:53,039
Those blueprints you left him for renovating

868
00:37:53,039 --> 00:37:55,119
or repairing the ancestral hall are still there.

869
00:37:55,320 --> 00:37:56,039
Not a single page missing.

870
00:37:56,199 --> 00:37:57,679
Whenever you decide which relative to pass them to,

871
00:37:57,880 --> 00:37:58,519
they're still good to use.

872
00:37:59,000 --> 00:38:00,440
Someone went out to the countryside to check.

873
00:38:03,760 --> 00:38:05,760
The money stashed in the flowerpots is intact too.

874
00:38:06,280 --> 00:38:08,039
Rats and termites haven't ruined it.

875
00:38:19,719 --> 00:38:20,519
It's a bit sour, isn't it?

876
00:38:21,760 --> 00:38:23,320
Taste it and see how you like it.

877
00:38:23,599 --> 00:38:24,000
If not,

878
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:25,199
I'll get you a different brand tomorrow.

879
00:38:28,400 --> 00:38:29,039
People...

880
00:38:29,960 --> 00:38:30,960
that's just the way it goes.

881
00:38:32,079 --> 00:38:33,920
Feasting guests in high towers yesterday,

882
00:38:34,079 --> 00:38:35,280
a prisoner behind bars today.

883
00:38:36,440 --> 00:38:37,840
Sometimes they never see it coming.

884
00:38:38,039 --> 00:38:39,800
Sometimes they do, but can't help it.

885
00:38:40,039 --> 00:38:41,119
It's just like driving.

886
00:38:41,480 --> 00:38:42,440
With too much momentum,

887
00:38:42,559 --> 00:38:43,360
you can no longer turn back.

888
00:38:45,920 --> 00:38:47,519
You're not someone who acts blindly.

889
00:38:48,119 --> 00:38:49,039
You know your own mind,

890
00:38:49,039 --> 00:38:50,039
and you stay composed.

891
00:38:50,559 --> 00:38:52,239
You knew when to hit the brakes.

892
00:38:52,800 --> 00:38:53,719
Yet you didn't.

893
00:38:54,400 --> 00:38:56,400
You certainly considered the cost of crashing.

894
00:38:56,800 --> 00:38:58,039
You weighed the pros and cons and ran the numbers.

895
00:38:58,440 --> 00:38:59,679
You studied mathematics, after all.

896
00:39:00,440 --> 00:39:01,960
All that talk about national righteousness

897
00:39:02,079 --> 00:39:03,519
was just a trade of interests.

898
00:39:04,360 --> 00:39:05,320
If I were in your shoes,

899
00:39:05,320 --> 00:39:06,159
I'd do the math too.

900
00:39:17,199 --> 00:39:18,280
All that talk about peace,

901
00:39:18,599 --> 00:39:19,679
and preventing war...

902
00:39:19,840 --> 00:39:21,000
These "Taiwan independence" lies—

903
00:39:21,000 --> 00:39:22,079
don't even bother saying them.

904
00:39:22,079 --> 00:39:23,159
You don't need their

905
00:39:23,159 --> 00:39:24,559
self-hypnotic delusions.

906
00:39:25,239 --> 00:39:27,280
Science is about seeking truth from facts.

907
00:39:28,960 --> 00:39:30,679
Let's stick to reality.

908
00:39:31,519 --> 00:39:32,840
In this generation of the Cao family,

909
00:39:34,159 --> 00:39:36,039
Cao Xiao'ou is the only male heir.

910
00:39:37,280 --> 00:39:39,599
An ancestral hall isn't enough; you need an heir.

911
00:39:40,480 --> 00:39:41,719
I looked into it for you.

912
00:39:42,119 --> 00:39:44,039
That clinic you keep visiting is a fraud.

913
00:39:44,320 --> 00:39:46,079
Don't buy into the fake banners on their wall.

914
00:39:46,599 --> 00:39:47,880
Ask a few people who bought medicine there,

915
00:39:47,880 --> 00:39:48,800
and you'll see.

916
00:39:52,360 --> 00:39:53,559
That's just how life is.

917
00:39:54,360 --> 00:39:55,960
Nothing can ever be perfect.

918
00:39:56,519 --> 00:39:58,119
You're a genius at missile research,

919
00:39:58,599 --> 00:40:01,599
but you have a genetic defect.

920
00:40:10,199 --> 00:40:11,039
A family issue.

921
00:40:11,519 --> 00:40:12,400
You can't blame yourself for it.

922
00:40:12,719 --> 00:40:13,679
Infertility.

923
00:40:14,239 --> 00:40:16,480
You have it, and so does Cao Xiao'ou.

924
00:40:16,800 --> 00:40:18,159
You and your wife have no children,

925
00:40:18,440 --> 00:40:20,519
so you treated the nephew you raised

926
00:40:20,519 --> 00:40:21,559
as your own flesh and blood.

927
00:40:22,000 --> 00:40:23,360
You visited every hospital in the province,

928
00:40:23,599 --> 00:40:24,960
always looking for home remedies for him.

929
00:40:28,360 --> 00:40:31,440
Bloodlines are just like stashed-away money.

930
00:40:31,960 --> 00:40:33,440
Life isn't easy,

931
00:40:34,079 --> 00:40:35,360
so passing it down matters all the more.

932
00:40:39,480 --> 00:40:41,320
But everyone has their own script in life.

933
00:40:42,159 --> 00:40:43,960
Much of it is predestined.

934
00:40:44,760 --> 00:40:45,360
Otherwise, why

935
00:40:45,360 --> 00:40:46,880
did you keep going to fortune-tellers?

936
00:40:47,639 --> 00:40:49,000
You studied mathematics.

937
00:40:49,320 --> 00:40:50,360
Couldn't you figure it out?

938
00:40:53,000 --> 00:40:54,719
Regarding your nephew's genetic disease,

939
00:40:55,199 --> 00:40:56,800
the US has specific treatments.

940
00:40:57,079 --> 00:40:59,480
Before coming, I secured a channel

941
00:40:59,639 --> 00:41:00,840
for one bottle a month,

942
00:41:02,000 --> 00:41:03,039
just in case.

943
00:41:10,000 --> 00:41:11,079
They must have promised you

944
00:41:11,079 --> 00:41:12,159
to supply the medicine,

945
00:41:12,559 --> 00:41:14,559
and said they'd arrange

946
00:41:14,559 --> 00:41:16,039
IVF surrogacy for Cao Xiao'ou in the US.

947
00:41:16,480 --> 00:41:17,280
That's why

948
00:41:18,199 --> 00:41:20,880
you were so eager to send him abroad on visits,

949
00:41:21,000 --> 00:41:23,000
to take the chance to flee with him and the money.

950
00:41:23,400 --> 00:41:24,800
But the money didn't make it out,

951
00:41:24,800 --> 00:41:25,679
and neither did he.

952
00:41:26,639 --> 00:41:29,280
Your calculations didn't quite add up, did they?

953
00:41:36,559 --> 00:41:38,480
From the moment you sat in this chair,

954
00:41:38,639 --> 00:41:40,199
you had no dignity left.

955
00:41:40,880 --> 00:41:42,519
The things an ordinary person can do...

956
00:41:42,519 --> 00:41:44,800
Cao Liaoping, you no longer have the right to do them.

957
00:41:46,199 --> 00:41:48,280
Only I still treat you like an ordinary person.

958
00:41:49,000 --> 00:41:51,639
At least you still have wine to drink today,

959
00:41:51,679 --> 00:41:52,880
and meat to eat.

960
00:41:54,559 --> 00:41:57,400
Aren't you going to enjoy these final comforts?

961
00:42:25,119 --> 00:42:25,920
How is it?

962
00:43:08,440 --> 00:43:09,519
I'm Wang Kai,

963
00:43:09,519 --> 00:43:11,239
inviting you to watch the drama series

964
00:43:11,239 --> 00:43:11,960
*Confrontation*.

965
00:43:13,400 --> 00:43:15,320
Do you recognize anyone here?

966
00:43:15,960 --> 00:43:17,320
I only recognize this one.

967
00:43:20,360 --> 00:43:22,519
Pay up, or I'll cripple your right foot.

968
00:43:22,960 --> 00:43:24,960
What are you doing? What are you doing?

969
00:43:24,960 --> 00:43:26,320
Loan shark interest compounds until it ruins you!

970
00:43:26,320 --> 00:43:27,199
Don't you get that?

971
00:43:27,199 --> 00:43:28,440
And you're still defending him!

972
00:43:28,440 --> 00:43:30,000
When I say I can pay it back, I will!

973
00:43:30,000 --> 00:43:31,199
I think I'm losing my mind.

974
00:43:31,199 --> 00:43:32,639
The person Jiang Zaizhen mentioned...

975
00:43:32,639 --> 00:43:34,480
...is definitely right at this table.

976
00:43:34,480 --> 00:43:35,760
Now everyone looks suspicious to me.
